IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wica-tables`

-- Work Injury Compensation Act 2019 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition,
-- informal consolidation in force from 1 December 2025.
--
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/WICA2019.txt
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the text with the writing-l4-rules skill and
-- nothing else: no pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no
-- human gate. Observations, not checked findings.
--
-- SCOPE. s 7 (the employer's liability and its three exclusions) and the
-- FIRST SCHEDULE paragraphs 1 to 3 (how much is payable for death, for total
-- incapacity and for partial incapacity). The Act has 8 Parts and about
-- 333,000 characters; everything else -- the platform-worker Part 3A, insurance,
-- claims procedure, appeals -- is not encoded.
--
-- THE MULTIPLYING TABLES ARE NOW ENCODED, in wica-tables.l4. The first pass of
-- this encoding could not read them: the deposited WICA2019.txt shifts the
-- factors by one row at each page break. They were recovered from the PDF with
-- pypdf, checked for completeness and monotonicity, and deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/WICA2019.first-schedule-tables.txt. So the
-- compensation figures below are now computed from the employee's age rather
-- than from a supplied factor.

§ `Work Injury Compensation Act 2019`

§§ `7 -- Employer's liability to compensate for work injury`

-- s 7(1): "Where personal injury is caused to an employee by an accident
-- ARISING OUT OF AND IN THE COURSE OF the employee's employment with an
-- employer, that employer is liable to pay compensation under this Act."
--
-- s 7(4): "For the purposes of this Act, an accident arising IN THE COURSE OF
-- an employee's employment is deemed, IN THE ABSENCE OF EVIDENCE TO THE
-- CONTRARY, to have arisen OUT OF that employment."
--
-- So the two limbs are not independent in practice: proving the second supplies
-- the first unless the employer displaces it. That is the whole architecture of
-- the section and it is why the record below separates "in the course of",
-- "out of", and the rebutting evidence.
DECLARE Accident HAS
    `personal injury was caused to an employee by an accident` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accident arose in the course of the employment`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is evidence that it did not arise out of the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 7(2)(a)
    `the injury is directly attributable to the employee being under the influence of alcohol or a drug at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 7(2)(b)
    `deliberate self-injury or deliberate aggravation of an accidental injury by the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 7(2)(c): injury in a fight or assault, with its own exceptions
    `the injury was suffered in a fight or an assault`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee did not assault anyone, or did so in private defence under Penal Code sections 97 to 106A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee was breaking up or preventing the fight or assault` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee was safeguarding life or property or maintaining law and order` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 7(4), as a rule rather than as an assumption.
GIVEN `the accident` IS AN Accident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the accident is taken to arise out of the employment` IF
        `the accident`'s `the accident arose in the course of the employment`
    AND NOT `the accident`'s `there is evidence that it did not arise out of the employment`

-- s 7(2)(c): the injury in a fight is excluded UNLESS one of the listed things
-- is true. The limbs are (i) the employee did not assault anyone or acted in
-- private defence; or (ii) the employee was breaking up the fight, or
-- safeguarding life, property or order.
GIVEN `the accident` IS AN Accident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an exception to the fight exclusion applies` IF
        `the accident`'s `the employee did not assault anyone, or did so in private defence under Penal Code sections 97 to 106A`
    ..  `the accident`'s `the employee was breaking up or preventing the fight or assault`
    OR  `the accident`'s `the employee was safeguarding life or property or maintaining law and order`

GIVEN `the accident` IS AN Accident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fight exclusion in section 7(2)(c) applies` IF
        `the accident`'s `the injury was suffered in a fight or an assault`
    AND NOT `an exception to the fight exclusion applies` `the accident`

GIVEN `the accident` IS AN Accident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an exclusion in section 7(2) applies` IF
        `the accident`'s `the injury is directly attributable to the employee being under the influence of alcohol or a drug at the time`
    ..  `the accident`'s `deliberate self-injury or deliberate aggravation of an accidental injury by the employee`
    OR  `the fight exclusion in section 7(2)(c) applies` `the accident`

GIVEN `the accident` IS AN Accident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer is liable to pay compensation` IF
        `the accident`'s `personal injury was caused to an employee by an accident`
    AND `the accident`'s `the accident arose in the course of the employment`
    AND `the accident is taken to arise out of the employment` `the accident`
    AND NOT `an exclusion in section 7(2) applies` `the accident`

§§ `First Schedule -- the amount of compensation`

-- The Schedule's amounts were raised with effect from 1 November 2025
-- (S 694/2025), and the Act keeps BOTH sets, selected by the date of the
-- accident rather than the date of the claim. No DATE type is available on this
-- toolchain, so which set applies is a fact.
DECLARE Injury HAS
    -- "AME" -- average monthly earnings, computed under the Schedule's own
    -- paragraphs. Not encoded: the computation has six sub-paragraphs of its own
    -- and several Commissioner discretions.
    `the average monthly earnings`      IS A NUMBER
    -- Paragraph 1(1) and paragraph 2(a): the factor is read from Table A or
    -- Table B "according to the AGE ON THE NEXT BIRTHDAY of the ... employee AT
    -- THE TIME OF THE ACCIDENT". Not the age at death, and not the age when the
    -- claim is made.
    `the age on the next birthday at the time of the accident` IS A NUMBER
    `the accident took place on or after 1 November 2025` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Paragraph 3: the percentage of loss of earning capacity, from the Fourth
    -- Schedule where the injury is listed there and otherwise assessed.
    `the percentage of loss of earning capacity` IS A NUMBER

-- The clamp the Schedule applies twice, with different numbers each time.
GIVEN `the amount` IS A NUMBER, `the floor` IS A NUMBER, `the cap` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the amount held between the floor and the cap` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amount` LESS THAN `the floor`    THEN `the floor`
        IF `the amount` GREATER THAN `the cap`   THEN `the cap`
        OTHERWISE `the amount`

§§§ `paragraph 1 -- death`

-- Para 1(1): "where death results from a work injury, the amount of
-- compensation payable must be paid in a lump sum, obtained by multiplying the
-- AME of the deceased employee by the appropriate factor in the second column
-- of Table A according to the age on the next birthday of the deceased employee
-- at the time of the accident".
GIVEN `the injury` IS AN Injury
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the unadjusted death compensation` IS
    `the injury`'s `the average monthly earnings`
        TIMES `the Table A factor` (`the injury`'s `the age on the next birthday at the time of the accident`)

-- Para 1(2): accident before 1 November 2025 -- floor $76,000, cap $225,000.
-- Para 1(3): accident on or after -- floor $91,000, cap $269,000.
GIVEN `the injury` IS AN Injury
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the death compensation floor` IS
    IF `the injury`'s `the accident took place on or after 1 November 2025` THEN 91000 ELSE 76000

GIVEN `the injury` IS AN Injury
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the death compensation cap` IS
    IF `the injury`'s `the accident took place on or after 1 November 2025` THEN 269000 ELSE 225000

GIVEN `the injury` IS AN Injury
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the compensation for death` IS
    `the amount held between the floor and the cap`
        (`the unadjusted death compensation` `the injury`)
        (`the death compensation floor` `the injury`)
        (`the death compensation cap` `the injury`)

§§§ `paragraph 2 -- permanent or current total incapacity`

-- Para 2: "the amount of compensation calculated in accordance with the formula
-- C + 0.25C must be paid in a lump sum, where C is -- (a) ... AME ... multiplied
-- by the appropriate factor in ... Table B ...; (b) where the accident takes
-- place before 1 November 2025 -- (i) if the amount obtained under
-- sub-paragraph (a) is less than $97,000 -- $97,000; or (ii) if ... more than
-- $289,000 -- $289,000; and (c) where the accident takes place on or after
-- 1 November 2025 -- (i) ... less than $116,000 -- $116,000; or (ii) ... more
-- than $346,000 -- $346,000."
--
-- NOTE THE ORDER. The floor and the cap bite on C, which is the product BEFORE
-- the formula is applied. So the uplift of a quarter is applied to the clamped
-- figure, and the final sum can exceed the stated cap by 25%.
GIVEN `the injury` IS AN Injury
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the total incapacity floor` IS
    IF `the injury`'s `the accident took place on or after 1 November 2025` THEN 116000 ELSE 97000

GIVEN `the injury` IS AN Injury
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the total incapacity cap` IS
    IF `the injury`'s `the accident took place on or after 1 November 2025` THEN 346000 ELSE 289000

-- C, as the Schedule defines it: the product, then clamped.
GIVEN `the injury` IS AN Injury
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `C` IS
    `the amount held between the floor and the cap`
        (`the injury`'s `the average monthly earnings`
            TIMES `the Table B factor` (`the injury`'s `the age on the next birthday at the time of the accident`))
        (`the total incapacity floor` `the injury`)
        (`the total incapacity cap` `the injury`)

-- C + 0.25C.
GIVEN `the injury` IS AN Injury
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the compensation for total incapacity` IS
    `C` `the injury` PLUS (0.25 TIMES (`C` `the injury`))

§§§ `paragraph 3 -- permanent or current partial incapacity`

-- Para 3(1): "the amount of compensation is to be calculated -- (a) in the case
-- of an injury specified in the Fourth Schedule -- by multiplying C (mentioned
-- in paragraph 2) by the percentage of loss of earning capacity caused by the
-- injury as specified in that Schedule; and (b) in the case of an injury not
-- specified in the Fourth Schedule -- by multiplying C ... by the percentage of
-- loss of earning capacity ... in every employment which the employee was
-- capable of undertaking at the time of the accident".
--
-- Both limbs do the same arithmetic; they differ only in where the percentage
-- comes from. So the percentage is one supplied fact and the rule is one rule.
--
-- IT MULTIPLIES C, NOT THE PARAGRAPH 2 FIGURE. A partially incapacitated
-- employee therefore does not get a fraction of what a totally incapacitated
-- one gets: they get a fraction of C, and the totally incapacitated employee
-- gets C plus a quarter. At 100% loss of earning capacity the two differ by
-- that quarter.
GIVEN `the injury` IS AN Injury
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the compensation for partial incapacity` IS
    `C` `the injury` TIMES (`the injury`'s `the percentage of loss of earning capacity`)
